Tag verbosity/limitations?

I've been slowly consolidating and gathering my collection, and am starting to try to figure out what folders/tags to use to organize things.  The wiki examples are like "cartoons", or "news".  I'm curious if tags need to be limited to a single word like that, or can I do things like "news_morning" and "news_night", or "cartoons_saturday_morning" and "cartoons_disney_afternoon"?
The deeper I get the more I realize how specific my expectations are per day or time.  I don't want "sitcom" I want "sitcom_70s_rerun".
Another question is if I want a particular show at a specific time, do I just make a folder/tag specifically for that show? Or is there a different way to call those?  I'd mentioned in my previous post about things like The Price is Right always being on at 10AM.  (I feel like Rainman now - "Uh oh! 15 minutes til Wapner!")
Thanks though.  This has been fun so far, and I haven't even gotten up and running yet.

